    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "f9bfc8c4c2954e4509f3b97e1090ee23ec33f804",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1700: the world runs while you learn\n\nOwner, on a fresh character: \"all the background stuff under world is\nbroken, just tried to show it off and none of it works. the world and lore\nbuttons are on the minimap which no longer takes you to the big map\" \u2014 and,\nasked: \"completely broken on a new character, but it works fine on my old\ncharacter\". Both keyed off the tutorial.\n\n  - worldRealtimeTick returned early while tutorialStep was set. The guard\n    (arb-fix) predates OTA-958, which took faction standing out of the\n    heartbeat; since then it protected nothing and cost a new character its\n    whole living world \u2014 no patrols, no events, no power moving \u2014 for the\n    twelve-beat tutorial. Measured on the unfixed store: twelve heartbeats,\n    events 0, patrols 0, ticks undefined. The heartbeat now runs during the\n    tutorial; worldTideCheck (the in-game pulse, which does move standing)\n    keeps its guard, and the suite pins that standing still does not move\n    on the heartbeat.\n  - The minimap tap carried the old MAP button's lockdown refusal (OTA-1375):\n    buzz + Arbiter nudge, no Atlas. Reading the map was never the way out of\n    the scripted crawl \u2014 the Atlas's travel rows are \u2014 so the minimap opens\n    the Atlas and the two travel-row handlers refuse under the lock instead\n    (MapScreen refuseUnderTutorial: same double-pulse buzz, same nudge).\n  - isTutorialLocked(tutorialStep, tutorialExploreChosen) in tutorialSteps.ts\n    is the one rule; InputBox, ExplorationScreen and MapScreen read it\n    instead of each re-deriving it from TUT_LOCK_BEATS.\n  - WORLD, the minimap and LORE write `ui: tap \"\u2691 WORLD\" / \"map\" / \"\u25c8 LORE\"`\n    (the rendered label, ota1485's rule) \u2014 none of the three doors wrote a\n    line before, which is why this took a question instead of a log.\n\nSuite: __tests__/ota1700TheWorldRunsWhileYouLearn.test.tsx (9). ota1370's\nlock pin re-anchored to the Atlas; check:standingat allowlist line moved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-05T20:10:22Z",
